// Stopping a program on purpose. `panic(msg)` and `abort()` are built into the language; these
// are its common reasons, as functions that never return. A function can end with a call to one
// and needs no `return` after it.

/// Stops the program: code that should never run did.
fn unreachable() -> ! {
  panic("internal error: entered unreachable code");
}

/// Stops the program: this code is not written yet.
fn todo() -> ! {
  panic("not yet implemented");
}

/// Stops the program: this case is not supported.
fn unimplemented() -> ! {
  panic("not implemented");
}
